## Why This Is Asked
This question tests dynamic programming with multiple constraints: non-adjacent blocks, exact block count, and reconstruction requirements.

## Key Concepts
- Disjoint blocks with at least one-element gap between consecutive blocks
- dp[i][t] transitions for skipping elements vs. ending a block
- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sum queries
- Backpointers for reconstructing the chosen subarray endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const prefix = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) prefix[i] = prefix[i - 1] + A[i - 1];

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      // Skip element i
      if (dp[i - 1][t] >= dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
        prev[i][t] = { skipped: true };
      }
      // End a block at i
      for (let s = 1; s <= i; s++) {
        const prevIdx = s >= 2 ? s - 2 : 0;
        const val = dp[prevIdx][t - 1] + (prefix[i] - prefix[s - 1]) - c;
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          prev[i][t] = { skipped: false, start: s };
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruction
  const result = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (i > 0 && t > 0) {
    const state = prev[i][t];
    if (state.skipped) {
      i--;
    } else {
      result.push({ start: state.start, end: i });
      i = state.start - 2;
      t--;
    }
  }
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks: result.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Explores a DP variant transforming flips into max-sum of k disjoint subarrays on a simple gain array.

## Key Concepts
- DP with two matrices: dp for best total, best for segments ending at i
- Transform 0/1 to +1/-1 gains to linearize gains
- Reconstructing segments via parent pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOnesAfterKFlips(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const gain = Array.from({length:n}, (_,i)=> s[i]==='0'?1:-1);
  const NEG = -1e9;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const best = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      best[i][t] = Math.max(best[i-1][t] + gain[i-1], dp[i-1][t-1] + gain[i-1]);
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], best[i][t]);
    }
  }
  const ones = s.split('').filter(c=>c==='1').length;
  return ones + dp[n][k];
}
```

